cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Neural ODEs for dynamical systems"
abstract: "Neural ordinary differential equations (Chen et al., 2018) learn the vector field of a damped pendulum and of the Lotka-Volterra system from short noisy trajectories and are scored on extrapolation beyond the training window. An ablation compares an unconstrained MLP, the same MLP in log-coordinates and a Hamiltonian neural network, trained on one or three trajectories with the exact likelihood of the observation noise and evaluated on unseen orbits over five seeds."
